---@class posthog.organizations.CreateInviteRequest
---@field organization_id string ID of the organization you're trying to access. To find the ID of the organization, make a call to /api/organizations/.
---@field target_email? string
---@field first_name? string
---@field level? posthog.organizations.OrganizationMembershipLevelEnum|number
---@field message? string|distilled.Null Optional personal message in the invite email.
---@field private_project_access? any List of team IDs and corresponding access levels to private projects.
---@field send_email? boolean
---@field combine_pending_invites? boolean

---@class posthog.organizations.CreateInvitesDelegateRequest
---@field organization_id string ID of the organization you're trying to access. To find the ID of the organization, make a call to /api/organizations/.
---@field target_email string Email of the teammate who should complete setup on the inviter's behalf. Receives a PostHog-branded delegation invite granting admin-level membership on accept.
---@field message? string Optional personal message included in the delegation email (up to 1000 characters).
---@field step_at_delegation? string Onboarding step key the delegator was on when delegating, for analytics only.

---@class posthog.organizations.CreateLegalDocumentRequest
---@field organization_id string ID of the organization you're trying to access. To find the ID of the organization, make a call to /api/organizations/.
---@field document_type? posthog.organizations.DocumentTypeEnum|string Either 'BAA' or 'DPA'. * `BAA` - BAA * `DPA` - DPA
---@field company_name? string The customer legal entity entering the agreement (PandaDoc's Client.Company).
---@field company_address? string The customer address (PandaDoc's Client.StreetAddress).
---@field representative_email? string Email the signed PandaDoc envelope is sent to (PandaDoc's Client.Email).

---@class posthog.organizations.CreateOrganizationsProjectRequest
---@field organization_id string ID of the organization you're trying to access. To find the ID of the organization, make a call to /api/organizations/.
---@field name? string Project name. Must be unique within the organization (case-insensitive). If omitted on creation, a unique default name is generated.
---@field product_description? string|distilled.Null Short description of what the project is about. This is helpful to give our AI agents context about your project.
---@field tags? posthog.organizations.CreateOrganizationsProjectRequestTagsList Labels applied to this project. Names are trimmed and lowercased, and sending this field replaces the project's existing tags.
---@field app_urls? posthog.organizations.CreateOrganizationsProjectRequestAppUrlsList
---@field anonymize_ips? boolean When true, PostHog drops the IP address from every ingested event.
---@field completed_snippet_onboarding? boolean
---@field test_account_filters? any Filter groups that identify internal/test traffic to be excluded from insights.
---@field test_account_filters_default_checked? boolean|distilled.Null When true, new insights default to excluding internal/test users.
---@field path_cleaning_filters? any Regex rewrite rules that collapse dynamic path segments (e.g. user IDs) before displaying URLs in paths.
---@field is_demo? boolean
