---@class posthog.organizations.TeamFeatureFlagPolicyConfig
---@field require_tags? boolean When enabled, a new feature flag needs at least one tag, and a tagged flag cannot lose its last one. A create that declares it comes from a survey, experiment, early access feature, product tour, or web experiment is exempt, because those forms have no tag input. The caller sets that declaration, so a flag can still be created without a tag.
---@field blocked_hosts? posthog.organizations.TeamFeatureFlagPolicyConfigBlockedHostsList Domains to block from feature flag requests (/flags and /decide), up to 100. A domain also covers its subdomains. It is compared with the Origin header, or with the Referer header when Origin is missing. Entries are stored lowercase without duplicates. A pasted URL is reduced to its domain, and an internationalized domain is stored as punycode.
---@field blocked_ips? posthog.organizations.TeamFeatureFlagPolicyConfigBlockedIpsList IPv4 or IPv6 addresses or CIDR ranges to block from feature flag requests (/flags and /decide), up to 100. Ranges can be /8 or narrower for IPv4 and /16 or narrower for IPv6. Entries are stored in canonical form without duplicates, and an IPv4-mapped IPv6 address is stored as IPv4.

