---@class posthog.organizations.TeamMarketingAnalyticsConfig
---@field sources_map? posthog.organizations.MarketingAnalyticsSourceMapping Column mapping per external data source, keyed by source id. Tells marketing analytics which column holds campaign, source, cost, clicks and impressions for that source.
---@field conversion_goals? posthog.organizations.MarketingAnalyticsConversionGoalList Conversion goals to attribute against, in display order. Each goal points at an event, an action or a data warehouse table, and carries a schema_map describing which fields hold the UTM parameters, the timestamp and the distinct id. Replaces the whole list on write.
---@field attribution_window_days? number How many days back a touchpoint can be credited for a conversion. Between 1 and 90.
---@field attribution_mode? posthog.organizations.AttributionModeEnum|string How credit is split across touchpoints when a person saw several campaigns before converting. * `first_touch` - First Touch * `last_touch` - Last Touch * `linear` - Linear * `time_decay` - Time Decay * `position_based` - Position Based
---@field filter_test_accounts? boolean Whether marketing analytics drops traffic matching the project's test-account filters. Off by default.
---@field campaign_name_mappings? posthog.organizations.MarketingAnalyticsCampaignNameMappings Manual campaign name aliases, keyed by integration type then by canonical campaign name, with the list of names that should be folded into it. Applied before automatic matching.
---@field custom_source_mappings? posthog.organizations.MarketingAnalyticsCustomSourceMappings Custom UTM source values to fold into an integration, keyed by integration type. A UTM source can only belong to one integration.
---@field campaign_field_preferences? posthog.organizations.MarketingAnalyticsCampaignFieldPreferences Which field to match campaigns on per integration type, campaign_name or campaign_id. Manual mappings in campaign_name_mappings still take precedence.

